{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZqHRhL6p4JXymn3ZdCy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a clear picture. Let me move to the design phase.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** - Add error code for cancelled shipment:\n   - Add `SHIPMENT_CANCELLED` to the ErrorCode enum, so we can report when a cancelled shipment confirmation is attempted\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** - Add confirm endpoint:\n   - Add a new `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` method\n   - Take the shipmentId as a path variable\n   - Retrieve the shipment using repository.findById\n   - If not found: throw ResourceNotFoundException with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n   - If found and status is CREATED: update status to CONFIRMED, save, return with 200 OK\n   - If found and status is CONFIRMED: return as-is with 200 OK (idempotent)\n   - If found and status is CANCELLED: throw ConflictException with SHIPMENT_CANCELLED\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Add comprehensive tests:\n   - Test confirming a CREATED shipment transitions to CONFIRMED\n   - Test confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds without change (idempotency)\n   - Test confirming a CANCELLED shipment returns 409 with SHIPMENT_CANCELLED code\n   - Test confirming non-existent shipment returns 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Could create a separate service layer for confirm logic, but the existing code pattern shows business logic directly in the controller, so I'll follow that pattern for consistency\n- Could use a generic error code (e.g., VALIDATION_FAILED) for cancelled shipments, but the convention is to have specific error codes for each case\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Write | Response | Code |\n|------|------|-------|----------|------|\n| CREATED → CONFIRMED | repository.findById | repository.save(CONFIRMED) | 200 Shipment | success |\n| Retry (already CONFIRMED) | repository.findById | none | 200 Shipment | success |\n| CANCELLED | repository.findById | none | 409 + error envelope | SHIPMENT_CANCELLED |\n| Not found | repository.findById | none | 404 + error envelope | SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n- Test 1: Confirms CREATED shipment moves to CONFIRMED status and returns 200 with updated status\n- Test 2: Confirms already CONFIRMED shipment returns 200 unchanged (idempotency)\n- Test 3: Confirms CANCELLED shipment returns 409 with SHIPMENT_CANCELLED error code\n- Test 4: Confirms non-existent shipment returns 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND error code\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes. First, let me update the ErrorCode enum:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2396,"cache_read_input_tokens":22092,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2396},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0b58555a-5198-42d0-9cb3-11c0e6dd2fa4","uuid":"475e783c-9bef-4840-a504-26d0e130ea0f","timestamp":"2026-09-30T15:07:48.696Z","request_id":"req_011CfZqHRHnPDadKDxktr66z"}
